Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Import recognition and separation where their stages run

Reason: `finesub.stages` imported `transcribe`, `vad_asr_stage` and the
separator at module level, and all three load numpy and torch on import. A
run that resumes from an existing stable.json reaches neither stage --
`aligned_required` is false and the vocal stage never starts -- yet importing
`run_pipeline` at all demanded the whole ASR runtime. That is exactly the run
Nonoka X makes when the cloud has recognised the media and the desktop
continues with its own LLM: the launcher carries `[harness]` and nothing
else, and the run failed on `import torch` before reaching a line it needed.

The three modules are now imported inside the two stages that use them.
`run_pipeline`'s `model_name` and `gap_sec` defaulted to `transcribe`'s
constants, which evaluated that import at definition time; they default to
`None` and resolve to the same constants where recognition runs, so the
values stay single-sourced. Every other path behaves as upstream: a run that
recognises imports the same modules, one stage later.

Removal: Delete once upstream's `finesub.stages` imports without torch.

